From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:14:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l41: keep the ASP word length within 24 bits

cs35l41_pcm_hw_params() writes params_width() into both the ASP slot
width (ASP_WIDTH_RX/TX) and the received/transmitted word length
(ASP_RX_WL/ASP_TX_WL). For a 32-bit sample format that puts 32 into the
word-length fields, which only take 12 to 24 bits. On a TDM bus with
32-bit slots (S32_LE, as the Pixel 7 Pro's audio DSP drives it) the
amplifier then runs with SP_RX_WL = 0x20 (read back on the phone).

Program the slot width from params_physical_width() and clamp the word
length to 24, so a 32-bit sample is received as its 24 most significant
bits. This is what the HDA configuration of this part already does
(32-bit slots, 24-bit words) and what Google's GPL cs35l41 driver for
this phone does in hw_params.

For S24_LE (24 valid bits in a 32-bit container) the slot width becomes
32 rather than 24, which matches the format's physical width.

Evidence: static on the Pixel 7 Pro's bottom speaker at every gain, which
scales with digital volume and analog gain, and remains with the
protection DSP bypassed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
index ad55889c4..7eeceabcc 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
@@ -758,7 +758,7 @@ static int cs35l41_pcm_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 {
 	struct cs35l41_private *cs35l41 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(dai->component);
 	unsigned int rate = params_rate(params);
-	u8 asp_wl;
+	u8 asp_width, asp_wl;
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(cs35l41_fs_rates); i++) {
@@ -771,7 +771,13 @@ static int cs35l41_pcm_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	asp_wl = params_width(params);
+	/*
+	 * ASP_RX_WL and ASP_TX_WL take 12 to 24 bits; the slot can be wider.
+	 * A 32-bit sample in a 32-bit slot is received as its 24 most
+	 * significant bits, as the HDA configuration of this part does.
+	 */
+	asp_width = params_physical_width(params);
+	asp_wl = min(params_width(params), 24);
 
 	regmap_update_bits(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_GLOBAL_CLK_CTRL,
 			   CS35L41_GLOBAL_FS_MASK,
@@ -780,14 +786,14 @@ static int cs35l41_pcm_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
 		regmap_update_bits(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_SP_FORMAT,
 				   CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_RX_MASK,
-				   asp_wl << CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_RX_SHIFT);
+				   asp_width << CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_RX_SHIFT);
 		regmap_update_bits(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_SP_RX_WL,
 				   CS35L41_ASP_RX_WL_MASK,
 				   asp_wl << CS35L41_ASP_RX_WL_SHIFT);
 	} else {
 		regmap_update_bits(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_SP_FORMAT,
 				   CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_TX_MASK,
-				   asp_wl << CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_TX_SHIFT);
+				   asp_width << CS35L41_ASP_WIDTH_TX_SHIFT);
 		regmap_update_bits(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_SP_TX_WL,
 				   CS35L41_ASP_TX_WL_MASK,
 				   asp_wl << CS35L41_ASP_TX_WL_SHIFT);
